    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0508" n="461" xml:id="pg461"/>

                <head>333. Telegram 1033 from Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d333-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-11-02">November 2, 1955,
                        noon</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d333-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d333-1"/>
                <p>1033. From Johnson.</p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] correspondent has informed
                    me in confidence he has learned that CHICOMS here have told Yugoslav UNESCO rep
                    now in Geneva that they are very unhappy with Soviet maneuvers in Middle East as
                    it is spoiling atmosphere for working out their plans in FE. CHICOMS are
                    supposed to have so informed Soviets.</p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] who is reliable believes
                    story is correct. My recollection is not certain as to whether Yugoslav was rep
                    UNESCO or other such UN organization.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gowen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
